{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>They have dealt corruptly with Him, not His sons.</b> That is, if a man corrupts his deeds and does evil, the corruption is not to Him — for He is not harmed by it — but to his sons is their blemish, as it is written: ״לא אותי הכעיסו כי אם אותם למען בשת פניהם״. And likewise the translation of Onkelos: ״חבילו להון לא ליה״ etc. And it is difficult to Rav Rabbi Moshe of Ponteise, for according to this it should have written שחת לא לו — the first without a vav and the second with a vav. Therefore he explained: שחת לו לא בניו מומם — their blemish it is, that the Holy One, blessed be He, says of them that they are not His sons when they sin. And so Hosea said: ״כי היא לא אשתי והם לא בני כי בני זנונים המה״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:44.030664633Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}